    {
      "step_index": 9,
      "thought": "I have the hero_ids with Super Strength. Now I need to count how many have height_cm > 200. I'll use Python to bridge the two databases and compute the final count.",
      "action": "execute_python",
      "action_input": {
        "code": "import sqlite3\n\n# Get hero_ids with Super Strength from hero_power.db\nconn1 = sqlite3.connect('db/hero_power.db')\ncursor1 = conn1.cursor()\ncursor1.execute('SELECT DISTINCT hero_id FROM hero_power WHERE power_id = 18')\nhero_ids = [row[0] for row in cursor1.fetchall()]\nconn1.close()\n\n# Query scanned database for height > 200\nconn2 = sqlite3.connect('/tmp/data_agent_structured_5ywi1uoq.sqlite')\ncursor2 = conn2.cursor()\nplaceholders = ','.join(['?' for _ in hero_ids])\ncursor2.execute(f'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM superhero WHERE id IN ({placeholders}) AND CAST(height_cm AS INTEGER) > 200', hero_ids)\ncount = cursor2.fetchone()[0]\nconn2.close()\n\nprint(count)\n",
        "limit": 200
      },
      "raw_response": "```json\n{\"thought\":\"I have the hero_ids with Super Strength. Now I need to count how many have height_cm > 200. I'll use Python to bridge the two databases and compute the final count.\",\"action\":\"execute_python\",\"action_input\":{\"code\":\"import sqlite3\\n\\n# Get hero_ids with Super Strength from hero_power.db\\nconn1 = sqlite3.connect('db/hero_power.db')\\ncursor1 = conn1.cursor()\\ncursor1.execute('SELECT DISTINCT hero_id FROM hero_power WHERE power_id = 18')\\nhero_ids = [row[0] for row in cursor1.fetchall()]\\nconn1.close()\\n\\n# Query scanned database for height > 200\\nconn2 = sqlite3.connect('/tmp/data_agent_structured_5ywi1uoq.sqlite')\\ncursor2 = conn2.cursor()\\nplaceholders = ','.join(['?' for _ in hero_ids])\\ncursor2.execute(f'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM superhero WHERE id IN ({placeholders}) AND CAST(height_cm AS INTEGER) > 200', hero_ids)\\ncount = cursor2.fetchone()[0]\\nconn2.close()\\n\\nprint(count)\\n\",\"limit\":200}}\n```",
